```c
vport = new_vport(&parms);
if (IS_ERR(vport)) {
    err = PTR_ERR(vport);
    ...
    goto err_unlock_and_destroy_meters;
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs when the `new_vport()` function fails, returning an error pointer. In this case, the code jumps to the `err_unlock_and_destroy_meters` label without freeing the previously allocated `upcall_portids` array, leading to a memory leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
err_destroy_portids:
	kfree(rcu_dereference_raw(dp->upcall_portids));
```
Reason:
The patch adds a new error handling label `err_destroy_portids` that frees the allocated memory for `upcall_portids` when `new_vport()` fails. This ensures that the memory is properly released, preventing the memory leak.

